              <h1 class="text-center fw-bold top-banner-heading-1 mb-5 mt-2" data-aos="fade-up">Clarisco's Refund
                Policy</h1>

              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">
                Last Updated: May 28, 2026
              </h3>
              <p class="mb-3" data-aos="fade-up">This Refund Policy governs all transactions made with
                Clarisco Solutions, including software products, custom development projects, consulting services, and
                related digital offerings. By making a purchase or engaging our services, you acknowledge that you have
                read, understood, and agreed to all terms in this policy.</p>
              <p class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">Clients are strongly urged to review all product demos,
                documentation, and project scopes thoroughly before making any purchase or initiating any project.
                Placing an order or signing a project agreement signifies that the product or service aligns with your
                requirements and that you agree to this Refund Policy in its entirety.</p>
              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">
                Scope of This Policy
              </h3>
              <p class="mb-2" data-aos="fade-up">This policy applies to all services and offerings provided by Clarisco
                Solutions, including:</p>
              <ul class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">
                <li>Ready-made software products and script licenses</li>
                <li>Custom software, web, and mobile application development</li>
                <li>Blockchain, AI, and emerging technology solutions</li>
                <li>Consulting and advisory services</li>
                <li>Support, maintenance, and subscription plans</li>
                <li>Third-party integrations and API-based implementations</li>
              </ul>
              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">
                General Refund Policy
              </h3>
              <p class="mb-3" data-aos="fade-up">All sales made by Clarisco Solutions are final. Our products and
                services are digital and non-tangible in nature, and once delivered, payment cannot be reversed. Refunds
                will not be issued under any general circumstances once a product has been downloaded, deployed, or a
                project has commenced.</p>
              <p class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">Clients are solely responsible for evaluating the suitability of our
                products and services before purchase. Clarisco Solutions provides fully functional demos,
                documentation, and pre-sales consultations to enable informed decision-making. Proceeding with a
                purchase confirms that the product meets the client's requirements.</p>

              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">Non-Refundable Circumstances
              </h3>
              <p class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">Refunds will not be issued under the following circumstances:</p>

              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">Ready-Made Software Products
              </h3>
              <p class="mb-3" data-aos="fade-up">The source code or product has been delivered via email, download link,
                or deployment, regardless of whether it has been used. The client changes their preference after
                purchase, including deciding not to use the product or switching to an alternative solution. The product
                performs as demonstrated in the official live demo and documentation, but does not satisfy subjective
                individual expectations that were not communicated before purchase.</p>
              <p class="mb-3" data-aos="fade-up">Issues arise due to the client's own server environment, hosting setup,
                browser configuration, or internet connectivity, as these are covered under our support policy, not this
                refund policy. The client fails to comply with local laws, regulations, or business model restrictions
                in their jurisdiction. Clients bear full responsibility for verifying legal requirements before
                purchase.</p>
              <p class="mb-3" data-aos="fade-up">An app is rejected by the Apple App Store or Google Play Store due to
                platform-specific policies, business model conflicts, or other decisions that are solely at the
                discretion of those third-party platforms. Security-related issues arise after delivery, as no software
                is entirely immune to evolving vulnerabilities. Refunds will not be issued on this basis.</p>
              <p class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">The client raises concerns about code quality after delivery. Code
                samples are available upon request before purchase.</p>

              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">Custom Development Projects</h3>
              <p class="mb-3" data-aos="fade-up">Development has commenced following client approval of the Scope of
                Work (SOW) or Task Breakdown Document (TBD). Once resources are allocated and work begins, refunds will
                not be issued for completed work. The project is cancelled or postponed after development has begun. All
                payments made are non-refundable for work already completed, and any outstanding balance for work
                performed beyond what was paid shall remain due.</p>
              <p class="mb-3" data-aos="fade-up">The client requests features, changes, or additions beyond the
                originally approved scope. Out-of-scope requests are separately billable and do not qualify for refund
                disputes. Delays occur due to third-party API limitations, external service restrictions, or
                environmental dependencies outside Clarisco Solutions' control.</p>
              <p class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">The final deliverable has been handed over as per the approved Task
                Breakdown Document. No refund requests will be entertained after final delivery.</p>

              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">Support & Subscription Services
              </h3>
              <p class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">Support packages or subscription plans that have been activated and are
                in active use.
                Any period of service already rendered under a support or maintenance plan.
              </p>

              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">Dispute Resolution</h3>
              <p class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">Clarisco Solutions is committed to addressing client concerns
                professionally. If you experience a technical issue or believe there is a genuine error on our part,
                contact our support team immediately. Our team will investigate the matter and work toward a fair
                resolution, which may include technical fixes, rework, or account credits at Clarisco's sole discretion.
              </p>

              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">Chargebacks & Payment Disputes
              </h3>
              <p class="mb-3" data-aos="fade-up">Clients must contact Clarisco Solutions directly before initiating any
                chargeback or payment reversal through a bank or payment provider. Unauthorized chargebacks will be
                treated as a breach of this agreement and will result in:</p>
              <ul class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">
                <li>Immediate suspension of all active services and deliverables.</li>
                <li>Revocation of all software licenses granted under the purchase.</li>
                <li>Legal proceedings to recover the disputed amount, along with any associated costs and damages.</li>
                <li>Continued use of delivered software after a chargeback is upheld constitutes intellectual property
                  infringement and will be pursued accordingly.</li>
              </ul>

              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">Third-Party Integrations &
                External Dependencies</h3>
              <p class="mb-3" data-aos="fade-up">Clarisco Solutions is not responsible for delays, failures, or
                limitations caused by third-party platforms, APIs, or services. These include, but are not limited to,
                payment gateways, app store approvals, cloud providers, and external data sources.</p>
              <p class="mb-5" data-aos="fade-up">No refunds will be issued for delays or non-delivery resulting from
                external factors beyond Clarisco Solutions' direct control. Clarisco will make reasonable efforts to
                communicate such limitations and work toward alternative solutions.</p>

              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">How to Raise a Concern</h3>
              <p class="mb-4" data-aos="fade-up">Clarisco Solutions takes all client feedback seriously. If you believe
                you have experienced a genuine issue, contact our team with full details for review:</p>
              <p class="mb-1" data-aos="fade-up"><strong>Email:</strong> business@clarisco.com</p>
              <p class="mb-4" data-aos="fade-up"><strong>Contact No:</strong> +91 94424 30551</p>

              <h3 class="mb-3 mt-4 fw-bold" style="font-size: 18px;" data-aos="fade-up">Policy Amendments</h3>
              <p class="mb-4" data-aos="fade-up">Clarisco Solutions reserves the right to modify, update, or amend this Refund Policy at any time without prior notice. Updates will be published with a revised effective date. Continued engagement with our services after any update constitutes acceptance of the revised policy. Clients are responsible for reviewing this policy periodically.</p>


